{% set local_problem %}
<p>Owens Cross Roads' rural setting doesn't protect homes from Alabama's humidity. Hot, humid summers create perfect conditions for rot. When gutters clog with debris and overflow — common on wooded properties — water saturates fascia boards. That moisture, combined with humidity, leads to rot.</p>

<p>Many homeowners don't realize they have fascia damage until gutters start pulling away or we discover it during an estimate. The paint looks fine from the ground, but the wood underneath is soft and crumbling.</p>

<p>Installing gutters on rotten fascia is throwing money away. The screws won't hold, and you'll be replacing those gutters within a year or two. Fix the foundation first.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Wood repair involves: assessing full damage extent; removing damaged sections; treating adjacent areas; installing new fascia using moisture-resistant materials; and prepping for gutter installation.</p>

<p>We use composite or treated lumber that holds up better in Alabama's climate.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
